  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thin disc of radius <math><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math> has a concentric hole of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> in it (see figure). It carries uniform surface charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math> &nbsp;on it. If the electric field on its axis at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>h</mtext><mfenced><mrow><mtext>h</mtext><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mtext>a</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math> from its centre is given as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>C</mtext><mtext>h</mtext></math> then&nbsp;the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/image24-293f48f3-e45c-4786-87cd-28362409a1c3.jpg\" /></p>",
    "image": null
